Non-Repudiation
In cryptogrophy, when someone sends a file, we make sure that the file is the same as it's original, the sender also sends us the hash of the file, When
we get the file, we look at the hash of the file we got to see if it's the same as the original.
Non-repudiation means you can't deny what you said, for example when you sign something, there is proof that you have read and accepted what was written
on the paper and you can't take it back.